Types of Social Engineering Attacks
1. Phishing
Phishing involves sending fake emails or messages to trick people into revealing sensitive information or clicking malicious links.

2. Pretexting
Pretexting happens when an attacker creates a false identity or story to convince someone to share confidential information.

3. Baiting
Baiting involves offering something attractive, such as a free download or device, to trick someone into compromising their security.

4. Quid Pro Quo
This attack involves offering a service or benefit in exchange for sensitive information or access.

5. Tailgating
Tailgating occurs when an unauthorised person follows an authorised employee into a restricted area without permission.

6. Vishing
Vishing is phishing conducted through voice calls, where criminals pretend to be trusted people or organisations.

7. Smishing
Smishing is phishing conducted through SMS or text messages.

Conclusion
Knowing the different types of social engineering attacks helps individuals identify suspicious activities and avoid becoming victims.
